  "fx": {
    "_comment": "specs.fx_objects. Base is each record's own rate applied to its native amounts, line by line on the running total so the lines sum to the rounded document total; a record with no rate of its own takes the latest exchange rate on or before its date. A receipt or payment relieves the document at the document's rate and moves the bank at its own; a note relieves its invoice or bill at that document's rate; each difference is on the exchange gains and losses account. INVE1 120.00, RE1 bank 125.00 FX -5.00, BILLE1 100.00, INVE2 12.51 + 12.52 + 12.51 = 37.54, CNE1 12.80 relieving 12.50 FX -0.30, PE1 bank -101.60 relieving 100.00 FX 1.60, BILLE2 50.40, DNE1 13.00 relieving 12.60 FX 0.40, IATE1 26.00 from the base side, JEE1 10 EUR at 1.2 = 12.00. Unrealized differences revalue foreign bank and party balances at the latest rate and are reported, not posted.",
